From e934e8c7eaa12135d1a100602194d4e2fc481654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: E3 <e3@nivxforge>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 03:02:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Open the EDR trajectory in a new tab, keeping the XDR
 incident open

A Process/Trajectory pivot used to replace the incident the analyst was
reading. Both XDR links into EDR are now ordinary links with target=_blank and
rel=noopener noreferrer, resolved through the configured EDR address, carrying
customer, endpoint, incident and the incident's OWN time range. The deep link
survives login because Protected already preserves pathname + search.

Two identities on one record is ambiguity, not a choice to make silently: the
control states which fact is missing instead of opening an unrelated device.

The EDR side adopts the named customer only after the server authorises this
session for it (the same authority the picker uses) and states a refusal rather
than substituting another customer. Two defects found while testing the real
cross-origin flow are fixed here: the adopted customer is re-announced so
surfaces that already resolved stop showing 'select a customer' while every
request carries it, and the canvas now opens on the link's time_start/time_end
instead of the last 24 hours. Nothing secret travels in the URL.
