From 57051d741511f5cece458702cc2f4fcfe4fd0bec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: E3 <e3@nivxforge>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:31:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] State an instant as an instant, and use a link range
 whole or not at all
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An incident whose created_at equals its updated_at describes a moment, not a
window. The link carried it as time_start == time_end, which the canvas could
not use, so it kept the stated start and paired it with 'now' — opening a
period the incident never covered.

XDR now sends `at` for an instant, and EDR opens the UTC day containing it —
the unit the canvas already navigates by. A start/end pair is used or ignored
together; a half-applied range is worse than the plain 24h default.
