From 7e40b040271cf5451bac5efd8c9bdd643fde928a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emergent-agent-e1 <emergent-agent-e1@nivxray>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:09:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Make the Timeline trajectory button open THIS incident's
 endpoint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The orange 'Open Device Trajectory' control on the incident Timeline tab
opened a context-free /edr/trajectory canvas: no endpoint, no customer,
no incident reference and no time range, for any incident at all —
including records that name no endpoint. It was the one trajectory
control on the record that had not been brought onto the cross-product
pivot contract.

It now renders the same OpenInEdr link as the incident header, so it
carries this incident's endpoint, customer, reference and time range
into a new tab, and says 'no endpoint on this record' instead of opening
a blank canvas. The endpoint itself is resolved once, by
incidentEndpointId(), so the header and the Timeline button can never
name different devices. The same correction is applied to the Endpoints
domain page, which navigated in-tab to the same context-free path.
